{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304523-exalted-analogues","id":1304523,"title":"Exalted Analogues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-12T16:19:12-07:00","id":1304523,"title":"Exalted Analogues","content":"So one of my hobbies is trying to link characters in other works to Exalted, and working out what they'd be if they were in Creation based on their abilities, history, and personality.<br /> <br /> Currently, I'm trying to do so for the entire roster of Smash Ultimate. Some of them, like Link, are easy. Others, like the Mother characters, were less so. And then there are some of the Fire Emblem characters, who I don't know enough about to decide.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10j72jZBfbwvxxw8f2IBuR8XpMQVPHLzve1slTbRuQ08/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Here's my current list</a>. Any thoughts on what I have? Opinions? And are there any other noteworthy Exalted analogues from other works you feel like mentioning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T16:57:52-07:00","id":1304535,"title":"","content":"Roy would be a Solar with fiery evocations on his artifact. Eclipse or Dawn.<br /> <br /> Ike is pretty much a perfect example of a Dawn Caste. (Even if I personally have made many Changing Moon Characters based loosely on him.)<br /> <br /> Chrom and Lucina would be either Dawn or Zenith Castes.<br /> <br /> I would argue Robin might fit better as a Chosen of Endings. But Battles works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/112-sanguine","name":"Sanguine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar112_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T17:56:49-07:00","id":1304545,"title":"","content":"I would argue that Link is not only a perfect Dawn, but a perfect Exalt, <i>period</i>.<br /> <br /> I went with Battles for Robin because they're a tactician.<br /> <br /> I should also note that all of my Exalted knowledge is based in Second Edition; I know basically nothing about EX3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T19:18:00-07:00","id":1304554,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d suggest telekinesis pushes the Mother characters toward Infernals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T19:27:39-07:00","id":1304555,"title":"","content":"Bowser and Bowser Jr have a couple of other options if you aren't married to Behemoth; they could simply be Beastmen, with one or both being a &quot;bad&quot; solar or an infernal (though, 3rd edition Infernal); or Bowser would be a Lunar with a Chimera beastshape (Turtle/Bull would hit most bits except the fire breath, which might be sorcery or spirit charms from consuming a spirit); or they could both be demons, with Bowser as a 3rd circle demon with Bowser Jr. and the Koopalings as 2nd circles. (With Koopas, Goombas, etc. as a variety of 1st Circle Demons underneath them)<br /> <br /> Ultimate!Zelda I feel could also work as Twilight, though since she's no longer Twilight Princess Zelda it's not as definitive. But I'll point out that Ultimate!Sheik is not the same person as Ultimate!Zelda despite them being the same in others - Ultimate!Sheik is based on Twilight Princess/Ocarina of Time Zelda (I don't think they nailed this one down to either) while Ultimate!Zelda is A Link to the Past. So you can easily make her a Night Caste like she clearly wants to be.<br /> <br /> Peach and Daisy might be Wood Aspects? It wouldn't be out of place, at least.<br /> <br /> If Luigi is going to be an aspect that isn't Fire, I'd put him as Air for the purpose of A) modeling his vacuum as a Jade artifact and B) replicating his Thunder Hand ability from Super Mario RPG.<br /> <br /> If we want Samus to be an Alchemical, Adamant doesn't feel much like her, aesthetically, and she doesn't do much Secret Policing. Soulsteel or Orichalcum would be my picks, but I'll admit I don't know Alchemicals very well.<br /> <br /> Pikachu and the other Pokemon could very easily be Elementals with some recoloring - at the very least, even the humanoid ones like Greninja or Incineroar are marked by their not being human and also acting as agents for humans. This would also allow for Red/Leaf to be Sorcerers with Summon Elemental as their control spell - they might even be mortal Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Pac-Man feels very... Behemoth-y, to me. Either way eating ghosts is a thing he's known for.<br /> <br /> Isabelle could be either a God or a Chosen of Serenities.<br /> <br /> Bayonetta is a No Moon Lunar, with some variation of Summon Demon as a control spell. She's too... moon-based, and does too many Animal Transformations, to be anything else. Her guns are a set of 4 Moonsilver Plasma Repeaters, with some amount of Jade Plating for the colors to work. Her spirit shape is a Butterfly or a Panther.<br /> <br /> Inklings are complicated, at least partially because they're a species and not a specific character, making &quot;Full Moon&quot; a hard sell. A pre-Primordial War race, a form of elemental, a race engineered by Solars in the first age, etc., all could work.<br /> <br /> Corrin is, in their original universe, a Water Aspect Dragon Blood. I'm not saying they aren't a Lunar now, just that at the very least, they were a Dynast.<br /> <br /> Shulk is a Twilight who invested <i>heavily</i> in the Monado's Invocations. (Before his Past Life showed up again and ruined everything.) <br /> <br /> Pit and Pittoo are easily done as Exigents of Palutena and Pandora. I know you don't know 3rd Edition very well, but Pit as a non-God agent of Palutena who she empowers directly, is best modeled as an Exigent. Dark Pit will probably have to be Pit's Twin or else Pandora's (Illegal) Exigence allowed her to create a clone of Pit.<br /> <br /> Meta Knight is probably a Full Moon with a Bat for his spirit shape. Or he's a Night Caste with several very specialized artifacts.<br /> <br /> King Dedede is the king of a Beastman Kingdom in the Northwest, or so would be my guess to explain his being a Penguin. Alternatively, he could be a Fair Folk with an obsession for being Kirby's rival.<br /> <br /> Ness and Lucas <i>might</i> be Dream-Souled? We don't know much about them yet but at the very least, it would replicate Magicant shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Depending on how well Umbral Exalted emulate Persona/Jojo shenanigans, Joker could default to them. Otherwise, he's a Night Caste Sorcerer with lots of Summoned Demons at his disposal.<br /> <br /> <br /> ... that's all I got for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4500-kuiperbelt","name":"KuiperBelt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4500_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T20:49:38-07:00","id":1304566,"title":"","content":"Link (especially <i>Breath of the Wild</i> Link) could be a Wood Aspect (makes great use of Archery, Performance, Medicine, Ride, and Survival) who favors Athletics, Melee, Occult, and two other Abilities (Integrity, Resistance, Thrown, or Stealth).<br /> <br /> Occult, because the Shieka Slate is basically a sorcerous phylactery, with each Shieka Rune being a spell.<br /> <br /> Dodge isn't such a priority in Exalted's system, especially when Link has Archery for the safety of distance and Melee for the parry and clash Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bowser could be an Anklok Dragon King, which definitely makes him rare, strong, armored, and fiery.<br /> <br /> King K. Rule could be a particularly thick-bodied Raptok Dragon King.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T01:45:46-07:00","id":1304592,"title":"","content":"I kind of feel like Wood Aspect fits Link better than Dawn.<br /> <br /> I mean, obviously in Zelda the main thing you're good at is fighting, but I don't feel like Link's main deal is he's a super-amazing fighter. Especially near the beginning of the games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T03:28:10-07:00","id":1304597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304523-exalted-analogues?p=1304592#post1304592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel like Link's main deal is he's a super-amazing fighter. Especially near the beginning of the games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guessing you're not one of those players who took down a silver Lynel in a goofy and arbitrary manner, such as with three hearts, no armor, no food or weapons, only a boulder?<br /> <br /> (I mean, I'm not one either.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T04:50:16-07:00","id":1304604,"title":"","content":"Afraid not.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... why is Mario a Fire Aspect? I remember how much fire and lava hurt him...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-13-2019, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T04:55:00-07:00","id":1304605,"title":"","content":"Fireballs. Y'know, when he eats a fire flower?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T05:09:27-07:00","id":1304608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304523-exalted-analogues?p=1304605#post1304605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fireballs. Y'know, when he eats a fire flower?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but only when he eats a fireflower.<br /> When he wears a metal hat, he turns metal.<br /> When he eats an iceflower, he shoots ice.<br /> When he wears a wing hat, he can fly (or gets a feather, or a hat with a propella on it).<br /> When he eats a mushroom, he becomes giant.<br /> When he wears an invisible hat, he turns invisible.<br /> <br /> His power is jumping high, punching hard, and being able to get a wide variety of powers out of strange items. He can't resist natural fire by himself, or do fire damage by himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T05:17:53-07:00","id":1304611,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to do this for <i>Der Ring des Nibelungen</i>, but I've been running into a problem: although most of the characters work fine as Exalts of various types individually, the whole thing falls apart when you try to fit them together.<br /> <br /> For example, Wotan seems to me pretty clearly a wolf No Moon; he's got the Tell, he's got the transgressive witch-king thing going on, he's got the protean nature, he's got the ungovernable rage. (Well, at least until <i>G\u00f6tterd\u00e4mmerung</i>, when he seems to enter a more Solar-type Limit Break.) Siegfried is a Dawn eight ways to Sunday. Hagen's a really twisted Chosen of Secrets; Alberich is probably an Infernal of some kind, though he might be a Getimian. (In 2e, he'd be a Defiler.) Siegmund I'm not sure about; perhaps a Fire Aspect? It doesn't matter, he's only in it for two acts anyway. Mime's an Earth Aspect; Freia's Wood; Loge's Changing Moon, though I'm not sure what his spirit shape would be. Nothung's probably a pretty straightforward Artifact 3, while the Tarnhelm is Artifact 4. The power over law and contracts in Wotan's spear probably puts it at Artifact 5, while the eponymous Ring is, of course, Artifact N/A. (The Tarnhelm and the Ring even have some Evocations named already.)<br /> <br /> Throw Br\u00fcnnhilde into the mix, though, and not only does <i>she</i> not make sense, but none of the other characters make sense anymore in relation to her. She can't be Wotan's <i>and</i> Siegfried's bonded mate; she can't be both a Solar <i>and</i> a Lunar. In her role in the story, she's pretty clearly Chosen of Endings, but her relations to the other characters scream &quot;not a Sidereal&quot;. And that's all without even getting into the fact that one of her major themes is how she gets her agency, her heroic protagonism, repeatedly stripped away (first by Wotan, then by Siegfried, then by Gunther), which... isn't really a thing that's supposed to happen to the Exalted, at least not in 3e, as far as I can tell; tragic is one thing, pathetic quite another. (Of course, it wasn't supposed to happen to Br\u00fcnnhilde either, but here we are with most of the cast exsanguinated, drowning, on fire, or perhaps all three. Along with the rest of the world. Welcome to Wagner.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Known elsewhere as Kurulham. Void where permitted.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/s/d34vnu2hx0ifmk5/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4277-jackson-mackenzie","name":"Jackson MacKenzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T05:29:22-07:00","id":1304612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304523-exalted-analogues?p=1304608#post1304608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but only when he eats a fireflower.<br /> When he wears a metal hat, he turns metal.<br /> When he eats an iceflower, he shoots ice.<br /> When he wears a wing hat, he can fly (or gets a feather, or a hat with a propella on it).<br /> When he eats a mushroom, he becomes giant.<br /> When he wears an invisible hat, he turns invisible.<br /> <br /> His power is jumping high, punching hard, and being able to get a wide variety of powers out of strange items. He can't resist natural fire by himself, or do fire damage by himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is specifically the Smash incarnation though, and in Smash he gets fireballs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T06:16:32-07:00","id":1304614,"title":"","content":"Fair enough then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T07:21:47-07:00","id":1304617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304523-exalted-analogues?p=1304597#post1304597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guessing you're not one of those players who took down a silver Lynel in a goofy and arbitrary manner, such as with three hearts, no armor, no food or weapons, only a boulder?<br /> <br /> (I mean, I'm not one either.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Link could be either a Dragon-Blood or Solar, depending on how the player and storyteller want to scale the game.<br /> <br /> A sufficiently advanced Dragon-Blood could pull off what you describe if the player is skilled enough. Such things aren't Solar-gated.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, if Bayonetta is a Lunar, I think her totem would be the Butterfly, as that's the form her shadow takes. I feel her Caste should be Full Moon, because she's an extremely physical character who doesn't tend to solve her problems in No Moon ways. She doesn't heal others, she doesn't make things, she doesn't mutate people, she doesn't create bolt-holes or plan ahead to always conveniently have the correct item to solve a predicted problem, she doesn't fight along side familiars, and she doesn't appease spirits.<br /> <br /> She can be a Full Moon and still use sorcery to summon and bind demons to do her bidding, and she doesn't even need the &quot;attack the immaterial&quot; Charm when her opponents become material on their own to fight her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T08:22:12-07:00","id":1304623,"title":"","content":"Link is the textbook Dawn, Solar, <i>and</i> Exalt in my mind. He's a hero, Hyrule's grandmaster-at-arms, reincarnating through the ages and granted divine power that manifests in a golden light. Now granted, my original estimation of Link's place in Exalted is derived from his Hyrule Warriors incarnation, who is <i>manifestly</i> the strongest version of the character. Also; Kirby might have more raw power, but Link is Nintendo's finest warrior, with only Samus being his equal in combat.<br /> <br /> I went with Infernal for Bayonetta, because her power is derived from a demon (Madama Butterfly; the giant hands and the shadow belong to her). The Mother characters are Infernals because, unless I'm terribly mistaken, all PSI is derived from Giygas.<br /> <br /> I made Samus an Alchemical not just because of her suit, but because <i>her very biology</i> is just as modular and open to modification as her Power Suit. I also went with Adamant Caste because she is so good at <i>everything</i>; combat, tactics, interactions with others, stealth, science... she is Nintendo's most capable hero.<br /> <br /> Also, I added Assist Trophies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":13327,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","user":"Voyd211","date":". 04-13-2019, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T11:33:13-07:00","id":1304649,"title":"","content":"Just because Bayonetta summons demons doesn't make her an Infernal necessarily; she also controls time as a major ability, which could point to Sidereal or Getimian. She just happens to also shapeshift is specifically into animals a lot, and has tons of Moon imagery throughout the franchise. Lunar sorcerer just happens to neatly fit everything but Witch Time, and even that might just be a spell or part of the Umbra Witch initiation, since it's just stopping time not traveling in it. <br /> <br /> (Also I hadn't even thought of her Shadow being her tell, but honestly that'd be super cool...)<br /> <br /> Makes sense for the Earthbound kids, but I still don't think Adamant specifically jives with Samus's aesthetic or MO. She doesn't do much with crystals or with being a stealthy undercover cop. She's a spec ops into Blight Zones, clearly, but not one that needs or wants to be undercover. <br /> <br /> For Assists, though:<br /> <br /> Skull Kid is a wood elemental, currently possessed by a third circle demon in the form of a Mask. (Or to pull out an old 2e homebrew based explicitly on Majora/Skull Kid: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/230892-re-posting-group-project-achsam-the-mask-of-unbrazen-pyrite\">Achsam</a>)<br /> <br /> Isaac is an Earth Aspect Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> Phosphora could be an Exigent under Viridi or an Air Aspect, or even an Air Elemental, to personal taste.<br /> <br /> Bomberman's role as a mascot and his color palette(s) would make me, personally lean Jade over Orichalcum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4500-kuiperbelt","name":"KuiperBelt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4500_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T13:45:47-07:00","id":1304689,"title":"","content":"Adamant caste Alchemicals aren\u2019t inherently good at everything. They\u2019re servants of the Divine Ministers, holy secret police keeping watch over the watchers.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d probably go with Jade or Orichalcum for Samus, depending on how much you want to emphasize her being a down to earth hero or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T14:00:47-07:00","id":1304696,"title":"","content":"Yeah, both Jade and Orichalcum seem to fit to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T18:54:29-07:00","id":1304742,"title":"","content":"Actually, I do not see Samus as Alchemical Exalted due to the fact that she is organic. I would suggest that she is an Earth Terrestrial Exalted with several powerful artifacts that each possess a number of unique Evocations. Her artifacts are her arm cannon, her powered armor, and her spacecraft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25244-the-fool-of-creation","name":"The Fool of Creation","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T06:28:12-07:00","id":1305253,"title":"","content":"I've got another big series to Exaltify: the Touhou Project.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know, most of the characters are gods or elementals. What I want to know is: which ones <i>aren't</i>, and what are they?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JURIwB2KKiPR339ObuhLBXDiHBkI-TDy2l-DkW68Eh8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the list</a>. I already have a few characters, but my knowledge is vague starting in Mountain of Faith, and ends completely at Unidentified Fantastic Object, so I can't really speak for the characters from games after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T07:41:48-07:00","id":1305265,"title":"","content":"Mai and Satono are Okina's current Chosen (Good luck deciding what Okina's god <i>of</i>, because she oversees a lot of things).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T07:44:19-07:00","id":1305470,"title":"","content":"Are there any Exalts in Touhou besides Reimu? Because seriously, f**k Reimu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Teller of Tales, and the Weaver of Dreams<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/14qUE6JyfwtXyd8SMY5gSJ_vvUZPCvGDZiIbBk19QPiU/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Behold! My 2e characters.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13327-voyd211","name":"Voyd211","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13327_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T09:48:53-07:00","id":1305503,"title":"","content":"<i>Touhou Possibilities (not exhaustive)</i><br /> <br /> <b>Hakurei Reimu:</b> Fire Aspect; Dawn Caste; Chosen of Battles; Exigent of the Hakurei Shrine's God<br /> <b>Kirisame Marisa:</b> Fire Aspect; Twilight Caste; mortal sorceress, possible Exigent of Mima, or otherwise bestowed with power by whatever Mima was<br /> <br /> <b>Rumia:</b> Wyld creature, possible newborn Raksha<br /> <b>Cirno:</b> Air Elemental (possibly the strange reincarnation of a Greater Air Elemental, to explain her curious strength)<br /> <b>Meiling:</b> ???<br /> <b>Patchouli Knowledge:</b> Air Aspect; Chosen of Secrets; Exigent of some god of sorcery, knowledge, books, or libraries; Second Circle Demon; (at a stretch) Third Circle Demon who is both library and librarian<br /> <b>Koakuma:</b> First Circle Demon<br /> <b>Izayoi Sakuya:</b> Getimian<br /> <b>Remilia Scarlet:</b> Changing Moon or No Moon Lunar; Infernal Exalt<br /> <b>Flandre Scarlet:</b> Casteless or Full Moon; Infernal Exalt<br /> <br /> <b>Letty Whiterock:</b> Minor servant goddess of the god of Winter<br /> <b>Alice Margatroid:</b> Demon-Blooded mortal sorceress; Air Aspect; Infernal Exalt; Exigent of a god of puppets or puppetry<br /> <b>Prismriver Sisters:</b> artificial hekatonchires made through necromancy<br /> <b>Konpaku Youmu:</b> ghost-blooded Fire Aspect; ghost-blooded Dawn Caste; ghost-blooded Dusk Caste<br /> <b>Saigyoji Yuyuko:</b> Deathlord or other powerful, ancient ghost<br /> <b>Saigyoji Ayakashi:</b> hekatonchire<br /> <b>Chen:</b> Wyld creature; familiar-god of a Sidereal Exalt; Casteless or Full Moon Lunar<br /> <b>Yakumo Ran:</b> familiar-god of a Sidereal Exalt; No Moon Lunar<br /> <b>Yakumo Yukari:</b> Chosen of Journeys, or Secrets; Goddess; Second or Third Circle Demon<br /> <br /> <b>Ibuki Suika:</b> Second Circle Demon; Infernal Exalt; Full Moon Lunar; powerful Raksha<br /> <br /> <b>Wriggle Nightbug:</b> minor Wyld creature; servant-god of some god of insects; sorcerously-uplifted insect<br /> <b>Mystia Lorelei:</b> minor Wyld creature<br /> <b>Kamishirasawa Keine:</b> Casteless or No Moon Lunar; Exigent or god-blooded child of a Hakutaku spirit<br /> <b>Tewi Inaba:</b> ancient Changing Moon Lunar<br /> <b>Reisen Udongein Inaba:</b> (not sure, except probably not a Lunar)<br /> <b>Houraisan Kaguya:</b> Goddess<br /> <b>Yagokoro Eiren:</b> Chosen of Endings, Chosen of Secrets; Twilight Caste; formerly mortal goddess of medicine<br /> <b>Fujiwara no Mokou:</b> mortal possessed by a Fire Elemental; Exigent of a firebird god<br /> <br /> <b>Medicine Melancholy:</b> minor Wyld creature; sorcerous creation; odd Wood Elemental<br /> <b>Kazami Yuuka:</b> Wood Elemental; Goddess of flowers, blooming plants<br /> <b>Shameimaru Aya:</b> Air Elemental; Dragon-Blooded Crow-Woman; Changing Moon Lunar; Raksha<br /> <b>Onozuka Komachi:</b> servant god of Eiki; Chosen of Endings; Abyssal Exalt<br /> <b>Yamaxandu Shiki Eiki:</b> Chosen of Endings; God; Deathlord<br /> <br /> <b>Aki Sisters:</b> Servants of the goddess of Autumn<br /> <b>Kagiyama Hina:</b> Goddess of Misfortune; Chosen of Endings, Serenity; Raksha; Second Circle Demon<br /> <b>Kawashiro Nitori:</b> Wyld creature; Water Elemental; Water Aspect; Changing or No Moon Lunar<br /> <b>Inubashiri Momiji:</b> Air Elemental; Raksha; beastfolk Dragon-Blood; Full Moon Lunar<br /> <b>Kochiya Sanae:</b> god-blooded Dragon-Blood; god-blooded Exigent of Moriya Suwako<br /> <b>Yasaka Kanako:</b> Air Elemental; Celestial Goddess<br /> <b>Moriya Suwako:</b> Earth Elemental; Terrestrial Goddess of the Moriya Region<br /> <br /> <b>Hinanawi &quot;Tenshi&quot; Chiko:</b> former mortal made a goddess; Sidereal Exalt","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-18-2019, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T19:04:23-07:00","id":1305620,"title":"","content":"To pick up where Sunder left off:<br /> <br /> <b>Kisume</b> is a terrestrial god of a well, or a water or earth elemental<br /> <b>Yamame Kurodani</b> is a Raksha or a spider-totem No Moon<br /> <b>Parsee Mizuhashi </b>is a God of Jealousy or a Raksha whose only mastered that 1 emotion<br /> <b>Yuugi Hoshiguma</b>, like Suika, could be a lot of things: a Demon, an Infernal, a Full Moon, or a Raksha - in any case, she's the same thing<br /> <b>Satori Komeiji</b> feels like a Second Circle Demon - the eye thing feels like great imagery for one, at least<br /> <b>Koishi Komeiji</b> is a demon of the same Primordial, whose eye was forced closed during the Primordial War<br /> <b>Rin Kaenbyou</b> could be a particular death-y No Moon Necromancer with a two-tailed Cat Totem, or a lesser soul of Satori, or a Hecatonkheir<br /> <b>Utsuho Reiuji</b> could be a Raven Totem Full Moon who found a very potent First Age Artifact, or a demon who artificially increased her power<br /> <br /> <b>Nazrin </b>is a Mouse Beastman Thaumaturgist (dowsing being her primary Ritual)<br /> <b>Kogasa Tatara </b>could be a First Age artifact, or a weirdly manifested Raksha, or a least god of an Umbrella that somehow became powerful enough to manifest in humanoid form<br /> <b>Ichirin Kumoi </b>is probably an Air Aspect with a bound Air Elemental doing most of her combat (Unzan) - could be a God-Blooded Sorcerer, however<br /> <b>Minamitsu Murasa</b> is a Ghost, but could be a Sail Supernal Moonshadow<br /> <b>Shou Toramaru</b> is an exigent of Bishamonten - God of Treasure, Tigers, and Warfare<br /> <b>Byakuren Hijiri</b> is a Zenith from the First Age<br /> <b>Nue Houjuu </b>is probably a Second or Third Circle Demon of Oramus, though could also be something even more alien - something from the Deep Wyld or even Zen-Mu<br /> <br /> <b>Kyouko Kasodani</b> is a celestial god of echoes who had to redefine her portfolio as people's understanding of echoes evolved<br /> <b>Yoshika Miyako</b> is a Zombie under Seiga's control, though could also be a Liminal she created (Breath might fit her powers and personality better, but Marrow feels more like Seiga)<br /> <b>Seiga Kaku</b> might be a Getimian - the Taoist Imagery and Weird Power fit - but could also be a Chosen of Secrets or a No Moon<br /> <b>Soga no Tojiko</b> is a particularly powerful Ghost<br /> <b>Mononobe no Futo </b>is an Earth or Wood Aspect - could also be Getimian (see: Seiga)<br /> <b>Toyosatomimi no Miko</b> is a Twilight from the First Age- could also be Getimian (see: Seiga)<br /> <b>Mamizou Futatsuiwa</b> is a Tanuki Totem Full Moon<br /> <br /> <b>Hatate Himekaidou</b> is whatever Aya is - an Air Aspect Crow Beastman, a Changing Moon, a Raksha...<br /> <b>The Fairies of Light</b> are all either Elementals (Fire for Sunny, Air or Earth for Luna, Water or Air for Star) or very low-ranking celestial gods<br /> <br /> <b>Wakasagihime</b> could be a Raksha, a Water Aspect Fish (Wakasagi) Beastman, a Fish (Wakasagi) Totem Changing Moon, or a Water Elemental<br /> <b>Sekibanki</b> is probably a Raksha or Hecatoncheir<br /> <b>Kagerou Imaizumi</b> is a Honshu Wolf-totem Full Moon<br /> <b>Benben </b>and<b> Yatsuhashi Tsukumo</b> are... the same class of being as Kogasa, most likely (Same for Raiko Horikawa)<br /> <b>Seija Kijin </b>is a Second-Circle Demon or a Raksha<br /> <b>Shimyou Sukuna</b> is the princess of a nearly-lost lineage of very small humans (Inchlings) with access to a disproportionately powerful artifact (the Miracle Mallet)<br /> <br /> <b>Kasen Ibaraki</b> is... whatever Suika and Yuugi are<br /> <b>Sumireko</b> could be a Mortal Sorcerer, a Twilight Solar, or a Getimian<br /> <br /> <b>Seiran</b> and <b>Ringo</b> are Rabbit beastmen under the service of the Lunarian Kingdom<br /> <b>Doremy Sweet</b> is probably a Dream-Souled, but could be a Second-Circle Demon, a Raksha, a Tapir Totem No Moon (with a lot of Dream Charms)<br /> <b>Sagume Kishin</b> is a god with a particularly nasty curse on her from Jupiter<br /> <b>Clownpiece</b> is either a very powerful First Circle (elevated in power by Junko) or some higher circle of Demon<br /> <b>Junko </b>might be a god of resentment, or some form of exigent, or an Infernal<br /> <b>Hecatia</b> is probably a Third Circle Demon - if not a Primordial in her own right<br /> <br /> <b>Joon</b> and <b>Shion Yorigami </b>are gods of pestilence and poverty<br /> <b>Eternity Larva </b>is a very powerful forbidden god disguised as a god of butterflies<br /> <b>Nemuno Sakata</b> is a mountain goddess or elemental, or an Earth Aspect Outcaste, or a Full Moon Lunar very connected to her dominion<br /> <b>Aunn Komano</b> is an enlightened terrestrial god or a Full Moon Lunar with a chimera totem (her Horned Dog thing) bonded to Reimu<br /> <b>Narumi Yatedera</b> could be a terrestrial god, a first age automaton, or a Raksha<br /> <b>Mai Teireida</b> and <b>Satono Nishida</b> are followers of Okina, either as mortal thaumaturgists, god-blooded, or even as her Exigents<br /> <b>Okina Matara</b> is a powerful secret/forbidden god<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4500-kuiperbelt","name":"KuiperBelt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4500_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T21:37:11-07:00","id":1305636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KuiperBelt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304523-exalted-analogues?p=1305620#post1305620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Parsee Mizuhashi </b>is a God of Jealousy or a Raksha whose only mastered that 1 emotion</div> </div> </div> </div>I could also see her being a ghost possessed by envy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Rin Kaenbyou</b> could be a particular death-y No Moon Necromancer with a two-tailed Cat Totem, or a lesser soul of Satori, or a Hecatonkheir<br /> <b>Utsuho Reiuji</b> could be a Raven Totem Full Moon who found a very potent First Age Artifact, or a demon who artificially increased her power </div> </div> </div>Both of them could actually be Fire Elementals, with Utsuho having gained power by eating the corpse of a Greater Fire Elemental.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Nazrin </b>is a Mouse Beastman Thaumaturgist (dowsing being her primary Ritual) </div> </div> </div>Could be a Celestial god servant of Bishamonten, which is pretty much what she is in Touhou; a divine mouse-person sent by her god to advise Shou and judge her worthiness. Like Jimminy Cricket, for becoming a Real War-God.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Shou Toramaru</b> is an exigent of Bishamonten - God of Treasure, Tigers, and Warfare </div> </div> </div>Byakuren might have used Solar Lore Charms to transform a tiger-themed Raksha into a god, whom Byakuren then introduced to Bishamonten as a potential new servant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mamizou Futatsuiwa</b> is a Tanuki Totem Full Moon </div> </div> </div>Changing or No Moon, certainly. She's a money lender, a tribal leader, and very skilled at transforming people and things into other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> I neglected to mention that Kirisame Marisa might be a mortal sorceress. Editing my previous post.<br /> <br /> I also didn't mean to suggest that Keine was a child of Tewi, but that odd cow-thing spirit with too many eyeballs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T22:12:29-07:00","id":1305640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304523-exalted-analogues?p=1305636#post1305636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Byakuren might have used Solar Lore Charms to transform a tiger-themed Raksha into a god, whom Byakuren then introduced to Bishamonten as a potential new servant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, &quot;a being created to represent the concept of a Tiger as envisioned by people who have never seen a Tiger&quot; feels <i>very</i> Raksha. But her being the &quot;avatar of Bishamonten&quot; also feels like its explicitly Exigent, especially with Bishamonten being very clearly a distinct being in relationship to Shou. <br /> <br /> (While I'm at it, the Jeweled Pagoda of Bishamonten is a really good name for an artifact - which appears to be made largely of Orichalcum with an orb of Adamant(?) in the center - though I do not have the Mechanical Mastery to start writing it up.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Some other thoughts on Touhou-As-Exalted:<ul><li>Fairies are, by lore, very similar to 3e Elementals - beings springing up naturally out of, and representing, Nature. Though a lot of Fairies are hard to pin down as any particular kind of Elemental, they share an origin story, so if you wanted to rule that as more important than the fairy's specific nature, it's a route to go.</li> <li>The abundance of gods in Touhou is probably a good introduction to how gods in Exalted works, to those unfamiliar with animistic religion</li> <li>A lot of Youkai are hard to directly import to Exalted, as Youkai are directly fueled by the power of Belief, which isn't necessary to the existence of most sorts of beings in Exalted</li> </ul><br /> Side-Note about Reisen: her Insanity Powers (which are technically wavelength powers?) and Lunar Symbolism (plus the Rabbit Thing) make me want to lean No Moon with a variety of weird Mind and Illusion charms, plus some sort of &quot;turn moonlight into a physical projectile&quot; charm for her original Yu Yu Hakusho-esque Spirit Bullets. (Eventually used to upgrade attacks from the Moonsilver Firewand she gets in Legacy of Lunatic Kingdom) Plus her backstory of escaping the Moon to attain her own freedom feels like a Lunar exaltation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4500-kuiperbelt","name":"KuiperBelt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4500_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T10:13:10-07:00","id":1305749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KuiperBelt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304523-exalted-analogues?p=1305640#post1305640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, &quot;a being created to represent the concept of a Tiger as envisioned by people who have never seen a Tiger&quot; feels <i>very</i> Raksha.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But her being the &quot;avatar of Bishamonten&quot; also feels like its explicitly Exigent, especially with Bishamonten being very clearly a distinct being in relationship to Shou. </div> </div> </div>I think it can work with Shou being a different sort of servant god to Bishamonten than the kind of role Nazrin plays.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (While I'm at it, the Jeweled Pagoda of Bishamonten is a really good name for an artifact - which appears to be made largely of Orichalcum with an orb of Adamant(?) in the center - though I do not have the Mechanical Mastery to start writing it up.) </div> </div> </div>I forget what the thing even does.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fairies are, by lore, very similar to 3e Elementals - beings springing up naturally out of, and representing, Nature. Though a lot of Fairies are hard to pin down as any particular kind of Elemental, they share an origin story, so if you wanted to rule that as more important than the fairy's specific nature, it's a route to go. </div> </div> </div>Ironically, elementals are the ONLY spirit in <i>Exalted </i>that permanently dies when you kill them the normal way, while <i>Touhou</i> fairies are supposed to be virtually impossible to permanently kill to remove the guilt of blowing them out of the sky in droves. But then, <i>Touhou </i>is supposed to be the sort of &quot;kinder and softer&quot; franchise which sweeps under the rug that youkai like Suika likely ate innocent people.<br /> <br /> <br /> The abundance of gods in Touhou is probably a good introduction to how gods in Exalted works, to those unfamiliar with animistic religion<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of Youkai are hard to directly import to Exalted, as Youkai are directly fueled by the power of Belief, which isn't necessary to the existence of most sorts of beings in Exalted </div> </div> </div>I find Raksha works well for most of them, especially the ones that hunt humans to eat them as a matter of nature they don't even question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Side-Note about Reisen: her Insanity Powers (which are technically wavelength powers?) and Lunar Symbolism (plus the Rabbit Thing) make me want to lean No Moon with a variety of weird Mind and Illusion charms, plus some sort of &quot;turn moonlight into a physical projectile&quot; charm for her original Yu Yu Hakusho-esque Spirit Bullets. (Eventually used to upgrade attacks from the Moonsilver Firewand she gets in Legacy of Lunatic Kingdom) Plus her backstory of escaping the Moon to attain her own freedom feels like a Lunar exaltation. </div> </div> </div>The Lunar Exalted didn't even get an equivalent to Phantom-Conjuring Performance, and never have. They have nothing like Reisen's ability to control or produce wavelengths, create holograms, or induce hallucinations.<br /> <br /> But I suppose Reisen could use the Swarm Charms for decoys and the fear-based Appearance Charms for inducing terror and panic. Mirror-Slip Trick seems fitting enough, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T10:39:24-07:00","id":1305757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304523-exalted-analogues?p=1305749#post1305749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then, <i>Touhou </i>is supposed to be the sort of &quot;kinder and softer&quot; franchise which sweeps under the rug that youkai like Suika likely ate innocent people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much 'sweeps under the rug' as 'doesn't dwell on it'; it comes up occasionally in the games and official manga &amp; books (<i>very</i> occasionally) that certain characters have killed/do kill.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}